.IX Title "YaraFFI 3pm"
.TH YaraFFI 3pm 2026-06-03 "perl v5.38.2" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
YaraFFI \- Minimal Perl FFI bindings for the YARA malware scanning engine
.SH VERSION
.IX Header "VERSION"
Version 0.07
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    use YaraFFI;
\&
\&    my $rules = <<\*(AqYARA\*(Aq;
\&    rule HelloWorld {
\&        meta:
\&            author = "John Doe"
\&            description = "Test rule"
\&        strings:
\&            $a = "hello" ascii
\&        condition:
\&            $a
\&    }
\&    YARA
\&
\&    my $yara = YaraFFI\->new;
\&    $yara\->compile($rules) or die "compile failed";
\&
\&    $yara\->scan_buffer("hello hacker", sub {
\&        my ($event) = @_;
\&        print "Event: $event\->{event}\en";
\&        print "Rule: $event\->{rule}\en" if $event\->{rule};
\&
\&        if ($event\->{event} eq \*(Aqrule_match\*(Aq) {
\&            if ($event\->{metadata}) {
\&                print "Metadata:\en";
\&                for my $key (keys %{$event\->{metadata}}) {
\&                    print "  $key = $event\->{metadata}{$key}\en";
\&                }
\&            }
\&        }
\&
\&        if ($event\->{event} eq \*(Aqstring_match\*(Aq) {
\&            print "String: $event\->{string_id}\en";
\&            print "Offsets: " . join(", ", @{$event\->{offsets}}) . "\en" if $event\->{offsets};
\&        }
\&
\&        if ($event\->{event} eq \*(Aqrule_not_match\*(Aq) {
\&            print "Rule did not match: $event\->{rule}\en";
\&        }
\&
\&        if ($event\->{event} eq \*(Aqimport_module\*(Aq) {
\&            print "Module imported: $event\->{module_name}\en";
\&        }
\&
\&        if ($event\->{event} eq \*(Aqscan_finished\*(Aq) {
\&            print "Scan completed\en";
\&        }
\&    });
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\f(CW\*(C`YaraFFI\*(C'\fR provides lightweight \f(CW\*(C`FFI\*(C'\fR bindings to \f(CW\*(C`libyara\*(C'\fR, allowing you to compile
\&\f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR rules from strings and scan memory buffers or files. It supports all major
callback events including \f(CW\*(C`rule_match\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`rule_not_match\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR,
\&\f(CW\*(C`import_module\*(C'\fR, and \f(CW\*(C`scan_finished\*(C'\fR via a Perl callback.
.PP
Currently it focuses on correctness and minimal functionality, not full \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR
feature coverage.
.PP
For more information, please follow the official documentation <https://yara.readthedocs.io/en/latest>.
.SH FEATURES
.IX Header "FEATURES"
.IP \(bu 4
Compile \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR rules from string
.IP \(bu 4
Scan in-memory buffers (\f(CW\*(C`scan_buffer\*(C'\fR)
.IP \(bu 4
Scan files (\f(CW\*(C`scan_file\*(C'\fR)
.IP \(bu 4
Events passed to callback: \f(CW\*(C`rule_match\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`rule_not_match\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`import_module\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`scan_finished\*(C'\fR
.IP \(bu 4
Match offset reporting for string matches (when enabled)
.IP \(bu 4
Rule metadata extraction (when enabled)
.SH "NOT YET IMPLEMENTED"
.IX Header "NOT YET IMPLEMENTED"
.IP \(bu 4
No support for YARA modules or external variables
.IP \(bu 4
Scan flags currently hardcoded to 0
.IP \(bu 4
Metadata and offset extraction disabled by default due to YARA version compatibility
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
Creates a new \f(CW\*(C`YaraFFI\*(C'\fR instance.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $yara = YaraFFI\->new();
.Ve
.SS compile($rules)
.IX Subsection "compile($rules)"
Compiles \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR rules from a string. Returns \f(CW1\fR on success, \f(CW0\fR on failure.
.PP
.Vb 2
\&    my $rules = \*(Aq...\*(Aq;
\&    $yara\->compile($rules) or die "Failed to compile";
.Ve
.ie n .SS "scan_buffer($data, $callback, %options)"
.el .SS "scan_buffer($data, \f(CW$callback\fP, \f(CW%options\fP)"
.IX Subsection "scan_buffer($data, $callback, %options)"
Scans a buffer/string for matches.
.PP
.Vb 5
\&    $yara\->scan_buffer($data, sub {
\&        my ($event) = @_;
\&        print "Event: $event\->{event}\en";
\&        print "Matched: $event\->{rule}\en" if $event\->{rule};
\&    });
.Ve
.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`emit_string_events\*(C'\fR    \- Whether to emit \f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR events (default: 1)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`emit_not_match_events\*(C'\fR \- Whether to emit \f(CW\*(C`rule_not_match\*(C'\fR events (default: 0)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`emit_import_events\*(C'\fR    \- Whether to emit \f(CW\*(C`import_module\*(C'\fR events (default: 0)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`emit_finished_events\*(C'\fR  \- Whether to emit \f(CW\*(C`scan_finished\*(C'\fR event (default: 1)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`enable_metadata\*(C'\fR       \- Enable metadata extraction (default: 0, experimental)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`enable_offsets\*(C'\fR        \- Enable offset extraction (default: 0, experimental)
.ie n .SS "scan_file($filename, $callback, %options)"
.el .SS "scan_file($filename, \f(CW$callback\fP, \f(CW%options\fP)"
.IX Subsection "scan_file($filename, $callback, %options)"
Scans a file for matches. Options are the same as \f(CW\*(C`scan_buffer\*(C'\fR.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    $yara\->scan_file(\*(Aq/path/to/file\*(Aq, sub {
\&        my ($event) = @_;
\&        print "Event: $event\->{event}\en";
\&    });
.Ve
.SH "EVENT TYPES"
.IX Header "EVENT TYPES"
The callback receives event objects with the following types:
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`rule_match\*(C'\fR     \- A rule matched the scanned data
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`rule_not_match\*(C'\fR \- A rule did not match (disabled by default)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR   \- A string pattern matched (emitted after rule_match)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`import_module\*(C'\fR  \- A YARA module was imported (disabled by default)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`scan_finished\*(C'\fR  \- Scanning completed (enabled by default)
.SH "EXPERIMENTAL FEATURES"
.IX Header "EXPERIMENTAL FEATURES"
Metadata and offset extraction are considered experimental and disabled by default
due to \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR version compatibility issues. Enable them at your own risk:
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    $yara\->scan_buffer($data, $callback,
\&        enable_metadata => 1,
\&        enable_offsets => 1
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
These features use FFI::Platypus::Record to safely access \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR internal structures,
but structure layouts may vary between \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR versions.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.IX Header "DEPENDENCIES"
.IP \(bu 4
FFI::Platypus 2.00 or higher
.IP \(bu 4
FFI::Platypus::Record (for metadata/offset features)
.IP \(bu 4
File::Slurp
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`libyara.so\*(C'\fR (YARA library)
.SH AUTHOR
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Mohammad Sajid Anwar, \f(CW\*(C`<mohammad.anwar at yahoo.com>\*(C'\fR
.SH REPOSITORY
.IX Header "REPOSITORY"
<https://github.com/manwar/YaraFFI>
